WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.634
-Welcome back to the show.
-Hello, Jimmy.

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:04.167
-It is always so fun to see you.

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:06.634
-It's so good to see you.
-I love hanging with you.

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:09.901
The series finale of "Black-ish"
aired a couple of months ago.

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:11.901
-First of all,
that it's a couple of months ago

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:13.400
is even crazy.
Where's time going?

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:14.667
-I know.
-Nuts.

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:16.133
-But it was beautiful.
It was great.

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:18.100
It was everything
that I wanted it to be.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.467
I loved it so much.
Eight seasons.

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:23.334
-Eight seasons.
170-some odd episodes.

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:24.801
-Wow. Do you remember --
Do you remember --

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:27.300
-Every single one.
-Yeah, no, exactly.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.334
You remember the one episode --

00:00:28.334 --> 00:00:29.667
-Yeah, I said --

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:32.133
-Do you remember the audition
was what I was gonna say?

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:33.901
Like --
-Oh, yes, I do.

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:35.400
[ Laughter ]
It was so funny.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.868
So, first of all, Kenya Barris,
creator of --

00:00:37.868 --> 00:00:39.300
-Genius.
-Yes, genius.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.100
He wrote on "Girlfriends,"

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.400
so I knew Kenya and he told me
he wrote this part for me

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.434
and he let me read the script.
I was so excited. I kept calling

00:00:46.434 --> 00:00:49.133
my agent, like, "Have you got
anything? Like, anything?"

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:51.067
And they were like, "No,
nothing." And I was like,

00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:52.400
"Seriously, though,
because he wrote it for me.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.334
So, like, that's weird.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:56.234
But that's okay. Like, maybe
it'll come in, it'll be fine.

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:58.267
So then it came in
and it was an audition.

00:00:58.267 --> 00:00:59.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:01.834
-The part that he wrote for you.
-Yeah, it's an audition.

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:04.434
-Okay, gotcha.
-So I go to the audition

00:01:04.434 --> 00:01:06.033
and this is ridiculous.

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:07.234
-That's hilarious.

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:08.901
-And there's all these
women there.

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:10.133
And I was tired because

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:12.133
I had flown in
and I fell asleep on the floor.

00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:13.801
And then I go in
for the audition

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:16.567
and there's Anthony and, like,
it's in a little theater

00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:18.701
and there's Kenya
and all of them were in there,

00:01:18.701 --> 00:01:20.534
everybody,
we do the audition.

00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:22.234
It was great.
It was Valentine's Day.

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:24.601
Anthony was giving out roses
like it was the --

00:01:24.601 --> 00:01:26.300
What's that show called?
"The Bachelor."

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.701
Like it was "The Bachelor,"
which I thought was

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:29.601
kind of charming.
-He's a charming --

00:01:29.601 --> 00:01:30.968
He's a charming dude.

00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:32.400
-Eh.
-Yeah.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.567
-Anyway, audition was great.

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:35.901
And then when we finished
the audition,

00:01:35.901 --> 00:01:38.033
he leaned out the door
and he said to all the girls,

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:40.100
"Go home! We found her."

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.767
-No, he did not.
-He did.

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:44.100
-He did not.
-But still, I didn't know.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.300
-Is that right?
-Well, because --

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:49.267
So I don't always trust it,
because early on in my career,

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:50.701
you know,
they do the breakdowns.

00:01:50.701 --> 00:01:52.000
And when you're an actor
that doesn't have an agent,

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.934
you follow the breakdowns
and you go -- and you --

00:01:54.934 --> 00:01:59.400
So there was an audition that
said "A Tracee Ellis Ross type,"

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:02.934
but they wouldn't see me.

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:05.667
-You're like, "I'm --
I am Tracee Ellis Ross."

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:08.234
-They were like, "No, no, no,
we're looking for a type."

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:09.901
-A Tracee Ellis Ross type.
-A type.

00:02:09.901 --> 00:02:12.033
"We don't want
the real thing."

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:13.300
Yeah.
-Is that right?

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:14.467
-That's right.
-Isn't that interesting?

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:15.801
-That's right. But, you know,
now it's --

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.200
I'm on "Jimmy Fallon."
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.567
-Yeah, exactly right.
Come on.

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:22.033
I mean, you've been --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:23.767
The show's received,
I want to say,

00:02:23.767 --> 00:02:25.501
like almost 30 Emmy nominations.

00:02:25.501 --> 00:02:27.167
You've been nominated
five times.

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:29.367
-I've been nominated five times,
yes.

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:31.167
-You are phenomenal in this.

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:32.701
-Thank you.

00:02:32.701 --> 00:02:35.334
-You know, I just saw you
present on the Oscars,

00:02:35.334 --> 00:02:36.901
the Academy Awards.
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:36.901 --> 00:02:38.667
-Yes.
-That was quite a night.

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:40.567
-Do you like being a nominee

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:43.634
or do you like being
a performer on the Oscars?

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:45.000
-Oh, I always like being
a nominee,

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.234
but I love
going to awards shows,

00:02:46.234 --> 00:02:48.067
mostly because I love
getting dressed up.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.100
-Yeah.
-I mean --

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:51.367
-You get dressed up
and you get to go

00:02:51.367 --> 00:02:52.567
to these amazing parties.

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:53.968
-You get to go
to these amazing parties.

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:56.334
Usually, you know people because
now when you're in the --

00:02:56.334 --> 00:02:57.934
if you've gotten to a point
of being nominated,

00:02:57.934 --> 00:02:59.601
you see your friends.
It's like really fun to do that.

00:02:59.601 --> 00:03:04.067
But also, you get to see
very exciting people.

00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:05.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.334 --> 00:03:07.901
-Like, very exciting people.

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:10.200
-Who freaks you out?
-I saw Brad Pitt once.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.267
-Oh! Now we're talking!

00:03:12.267 --> 00:03:13.934
Now we're talking.
-I saw Brad Pitt, okay?

00:03:13.934 --> 00:03:16.067
I saw Brad Pitt.
I don't think Brad Pitt saw me,

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:17.934
but I saw Brad Pitt.

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:18.934
-Wait, so you saw Brad Pitt.

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:20.901
-I looked right into
his eyes, Jimmy.

00:03:20.901 --> 00:03:23.601
And I was like, "Ah!"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:25.000
It was like -- It was like when,

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.300
you know, like,
if you see a bear,

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.634
you don't want
to make eye contact.

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:29.868
-Yeah.
-I was like, "[inhales]

00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:31.501
[ Chuckles nervously ]"

00:03:31.501 --> 00:03:32.767
Nothing happened.
Then he walked away.

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:35.701
-You felt all the feels.
-I felt all the feelings.

00:03:35.701 --> 00:03:38.767
Same thing happened --
Keanu Reeves.

00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:40.767
Oh, my God. Come on.
I mean, I'm 49.

00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:42.801
-People just heard that story
and they had the feeling.

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:44.400
-I'm -- I'm 49.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.434
I grew up on the Keanu.
I mean, get out of here.

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:49.100
You know what I mean?
Keanu Reeves -- like, stop it!

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:50.634
-Hey, just get out
with the Keanu.

00:03:50.634 --> 00:03:52.701
Get out --
-Brad Pitt, Keanu Reeves --

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:54.200
This is not the type of guy
that I usually date,

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.267
but whatever,
you know what I mean?

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:56.400
This is very exciting
movie stars.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.133
-Where did you see
the Keanu Reeves?

00:03:58.133 --> 00:04:01.000
-On a very small elevator,
Jimmy.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.767
Oh, my God.
I got on on the fourth floor.

00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:06.567
I think he got on on three.
We were only going to one.

00:04:06.567 --> 00:04:09.033
-[ Laughs ] But still --
-But when he got on,

00:04:09.033 --> 00:04:10.534
I was like, "Oh, my God."

00:04:10.534 --> 00:04:12.767
So, like, I held my breath and I
was ready because I was like,

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:14.834
"Oh, God. Here comes
the marriage proposal."

00:04:14.834 --> 00:04:16.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.133 --> 00:04:18.334
-He met --
It was a meet-cute.

00:04:18.334 --> 00:04:20.067
He ran into you, a meet-cute
on the elevator,

00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:22.200
and he just gets on one knee.
-I was ready.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.367
You know what I mean?
-Yeah.

00:04:23.367 --> 00:04:26.100
-So I like -- [ Gasps ] --
held my breath.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:28.701
And then I was like, "Oh, no,
no, I should introduce myself."

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:30.968
But then the elevator door
opened and he walked off.

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:32.734
-And he left.
-And that was it.

00:04:32.734 --> 00:04:34.334
And then, yeah, that was it.
So --

00:04:34.334 --> 00:04:36.601
-But Brad, were you more
composed with Brad Pitt?

00:04:36.601 --> 00:04:38.300
-No, no, no.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:41.634
Composure is not a word that's
used to describe me, Jimmy.

00:04:41.634 --> 00:04:43.434
That's not --
That's not the thing for me.

00:04:43.434 --> 00:04:45.701
-But you -- you actually
brought us a video.

00:04:45.701 --> 00:04:47.934
-Well, when I got
back hours later,

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:50.334
the energy was still
coursing through my veins.

00:04:50.334 --> 00:04:52.534
-Just so you can see
how much energy comes out of

00:04:52.534 --> 00:04:53.834
the great Tracee Ellis Ross,

00:04:53.834 --> 00:04:55.467
take a look,
after seeing Brad Pitt.

00:04:55.467 --> 00:04:56.667
-I saw Brad Pitt!

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:57.934
I looked in his eyes.
He didn't look at me,

00:04:57.934 --> 00:05:01.767
but ♪ ohhh ♪

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:03.934
♪ Ohhh ♪

00:05:03.934 --> 00:05:05.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:05.934 --> 00:05:07.734
[ Laughs ]

00:05:07.734 --> 00:05:11.167
-♪ Ohhh ♪

00:05:11.167 --> 00:05:12.934
I saw Brad Pitt!

00:05:12.934 --> 00:05:15.834
-[ Laughs ]
-I love that.

00:05:15.834 --> 00:05:17.634
-And by the -- I feel like
I turned into my mom

00:05:17.634 --> 00:05:19.667
in "Mahogany" in that moment.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:19.667 --> 00:05:21.968
-I was just spinning around
like life had begun.

00:05:21.968 --> 00:05:24.067
-That's so fun.
You made, like you said,

00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:25.634
over 170 episodes
of "Black-ish."

00:05:25.634 --> 00:05:27.601
-Oh, my goodness.

00:05:27.601 --> 00:05:30.133
-This past season, you co-wrote
an episode

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:31.501
that had Michelle Obama.

00:05:31.501 --> 00:05:33.934
-I co-wrote the episode
about perimenopause,

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:36.133
and then the first episode
of the season,

00:05:36.133 --> 00:05:37.934
Michelle Obama came.

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:40.501
-I mean, just --
-You know, it's like --

00:05:40.501 --> 00:05:42.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:42.234 --> 00:05:45.033
-That one about --

00:05:45.033 --> 00:05:46.234
-Which do you want
to talk about?

00:05:46.234 --> 00:05:48.667
Let's -- Maybe we talk
about Michelle Obama.

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:51.267
-Well, I mean, I don't mind
talking about menopause either.

00:05:51.267 --> 00:05:55.000
-Well, peri-- perimenopause.
Don't rush me.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:56.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:58.067
-But here's why I like the show.

00:05:58.067 --> 00:05:59.234
Here's why I like "Black-ish,"

00:05:59.234 --> 00:06:00.934
because you could be funny,
but also talk

00:06:00.934 --> 00:06:02.400
about serious issues.
-Yeah.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:03.667
-And you got that across
and that --

00:06:03.667 --> 00:06:05.100
you've got to be proud of that.
-Yeah.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:07.400
I leave with so much joy
and pride.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:09.434
The subject matter
that we touched on,

00:06:09.434 --> 00:06:11.200
the way we, you know,

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:14.734
gave America a Black family
as an American family.

00:06:14.734 --> 00:06:16.501
And, yeah,
there were so many things.

00:06:16.501 --> 00:06:18.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:18.434 --> 00:06:22.501
Really explored as a woman
so many different spaces

00:06:22.501 --> 00:06:24.634
and places
and anchored in the show

00:06:24.634 --> 00:06:26.734
was this couple that loved
each other, which I really love.

00:06:26.734 --> 00:06:28.067
We loved and liked each other,

00:06:28.067 --> 00:06:30.200
so it wasn't based
on that traditional

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.801
rolling your eyes
at your partner.

00:06:31.801 --> 00:06:32.968
-Yeah.
-That I loved, yeah.

00:06:32.968 --> 00:06:35.467
-Congrats on a fantastic
eight seasons, buddy,

00:06:35.467 --> 00:06:36.834
and thank you for coming
on the show.

00:06:36.834 --> 00:06:38.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
You're so good.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:41.334
-I really -- I really thought
Brad was gonna show up.

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:42.601
-No.
-No Brad.

00:06:42.601 --> 00:06:44.267
-No Brad. No Brad Pitt.

00:06:44.267 --> 00:06:46.067
♪ You didn't meet Brad Pitt,
you didn't meet Brad Pitt ♪

00:06:46.067 --> 00:06:47.467
But I want to show everyone
a clip.

00:06:47.467 --> 00:06:50.067
Here's Tracee Ellis Ross in
the final season of "Black-ish."

00:06:50.067 --> 00:06:51.634
Take a look at this.
-Ahh.

00:06:51.634 --> 00:06:54.968
I think we should sell
this house...

00:06:54.968 --> 00:06:57.767
and move
to a Black neighborhood.

00:06:57.767 --> 00:06:59.234
-Really?
-Really.

00:06:59.234 --> 00:07:04.234
Can you imagine if DeVante got
to grow up around successful

00:07:04.234 --> 00:07:08.367
Black men and women
that were not in his family?

00:07:08.367 --> 00:07:09.567
We've done Sherman Oaks.

00:07:09.567 --> 00:07:11.300
Like, we did it,
and it was good.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:12.667
It was great.

00:07:12.667 --> 00:07:15.100
I just think it's time for us
to do something new.

00:07:17.601 --> 00:07:19.467
-Let's do it.

00:07:19.467 --> 00:07:21.300
You have always had my back.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:23.734
-Always.

00:07:23.734 --> 00:07:26.033
-Mama was wrong.

00:07:26.033 --> 00:07:28.267
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:28.267 --> 00:07:29.968
-What?
-After 20 years,

00:07:29.968 --> 00:07:33.434
you finally figure out what to
say to turn me on, baby.

00:07:33.434 --> 00:07:34.934
-Oh!
-Say it again.

00:07:34.934 --> 00:07:37.901
-Mama was wrong.
-Oh, my God.

00:07:37.901 --> 00:07:40.067
-Yeah, that's exactly right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:40.067 --> 00:07:43.133
Tracee Ellis Ross,
everybody!

00:07:43.133 --> 00:07:46.901
All seasons of "Black-ish"
are available to stream on Hulu.

00:07:46.901 --> 00:07:48.367
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:49.300
Stick around, everybody.

